  "notes": "v22 changes direction from distance-extension training to a general-dogfight bridge. It starts only from the validated v21 iter_0001 native checkpoint and uses one mixed stage so the common curriculum trainer does not cross a stage boundary and replace native PPO state with a lightweight bundle. The scenario pool keeps 25% of the validated 900 m autopilot attack rehearsal, adds 15% of 900 m tail chase against the active AIP_BASE behavior-tree target, and uses the remaining 60% for mirrored alpha 0/20/40/60 geometries derived from the competition code's two-circle placement formula. Small position/attitude/ speed perturbations reduce memorization of one BT opening. The reward keeps v21's real firing-cone alignment, increases the penalty for ownship damage, strengthens rear-hemisphere ATA improvement for post-merge reacquisition, and removes tail-chase-specific absolute roll/pitch and 7,000 m hold penalties. Safety shaping now focuses on genuinely low altitude plus uncontrolled dive. PPO learning rate is reduced to 1e-5 and only two iterations are allowed; iter_0001 and iter_0002 must be evaluated separately, and the final bundle is not automatically considered the best model.",
